     9	EVALUATED at 64 (announcement 06; plan §3.1). At a batch of 32 those two caps
    10	partition the C4 orbit differently -- ``max(1, 32//32) = 1`` angle per chunk
    11	versus ``max(1, 64//32) = 2`` -- so they are genuinely different executions of
    12	the same sum, over the real DINOv3 backbone, on real AR data. If they disagree,
    13	the arm's training-time conditioning is not the thing its evaluation measures.
    14	Batch 32 is therefore not a convenience: it is the smallest batch at which the
    15	two caps differ at all.
    16	
    17	Eval mode is the point of comparison, not a shortcut: DINOv3's random RoPE
    18	rescale is drawn once per forward and guarded by ``self.training``, so in eval
