   502	    Full-C4 **Cartesian** frame averaging of every pose/geometry conditioner (exp_21).
   503	
   504	    :func:`invariant_conditioning` symmetrizes its two sub-paths by different
   505	    mechanisms — intrinsically yaw-invariant cylindrical features ``(r, z, dphi)``
   506	    for the pose path, a frame average for the ViT path. This method applies ONE
   507	    mechanism to both. The poses stay raw Cartesian ``(x, y, z)``, i.e. inside the
   508	    dist-embedder's training domain, and the whole orbit is averaged::
   509	
   510	        out[id] = (1/|G|) sum_g f_id(g . x)      for id in POSE_KEYS
   511	
   512	    over the panorama-aligned yaw subgroup ``G`` given by ``angles``. Every frame
   513	    rotates the depth panorama and ALL FOUR pose keys jointly (one
   514	    :func:`rotate_scene_metadata` call with ``pose_keys=POSE_KEYS``), so a frame
   515	    is a rigid rotation of the whole scene rather than of one branch of it.
   516	
   517	    The invariance class is therefore exact on ``G`` and on nothing else: an
   518	    off-subgroup angle is a genuine NEGATIVE CONTROL here, where the cylindrical
   519	    pose path was invariant at any angle. No scene-intrinsic reference azimuth is
   520	    computed, so the ``+-pi`` discontinuity and the meters/radians mixing of the
   521	    cylindrical triplets are both out of the picture.
   522	
   523	    ``context_audio`` — and any other id the conditioner produces — comes from
   524	    the single base pass. It is yaw-invariant already and may carry BatchNorm
   525	    running statistics, so re-running it per frame would step those statistics
